      "text": "If by **KL you mean Kuala Lumpur, yes—stay indoors as much as you can today, October 17**. IQAir reported a **US AQI of 204 (“very unhealthy”) at noon local time**, with fine particles as the main pollutant. For people with asthma, guidance at that level is to avoid outdoor physical activity. Readings can change, so check your nearest monitor before going out. ([iqair.com](https://www.iqair.com/air-quality/malaysia/kuala-lumpur/kuala-lumpur))\n\nKeep windows closed, use an air purifier if you have one, and follow your asthma action plan with your reliever inhaler handy. If you must go out, keep the trip brief and consider a well-fitting N95. If breathing becomes very hard or your reliever medicine isn’t helping, seek emergency care. ([airnow.gov](https://www.airnow.gov/wildfires/when-smoke-is-in-the-air/?utm_source=openai))",
